       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults (3,200 mg/day). Even 1600 mg as a single dose is well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute ceiling, usually for short-term use\n- **Something else**, if you intend a dose above the labeled maximum for a specific reason\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original 1600 mg QID, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note."
