       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but the reason you gave, timing around a family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose this high. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and more drug won't give more analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect. I can't see a benefit that justifies those risks.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range**, such as 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day).\n- **Add multimodal therapy** if pain control is the goal. Scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen gives more relief without raising the NSAID dose.\n- **Have you talk with pharmacy.** If there's a clinical reason for exceeding the labeled maximum, a pharmacist consult can document it and check it. The order can then go through the hospital's usual override process.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
